   "subject": "baseline colour",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p>How can I know what colour is used by default when colour is set to a variable? The baseline is pale red and by trial and error I thought it might be<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>hsv(0, .5)<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>For example<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>qplot(x = carat, y = price, data = diamonds, col = &quot;green&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>qplot(x = carat, y = price, data = diamonds, col = I(hsv(0, .5)) )<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>seem to be roughly the same colour. But is there a way to get a list of the colours actually used in a graph?<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p><p><u></u> <u></u></p><p>Etienne<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "H37fcVOqBcUJ",
   "from": "James McCreight",
   "author": "daf017f67eba24e8",
   "date": "2011-10-06T13:04:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: baseline colour",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>I&#39;m not totally sure what you want but you can look in here</div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/scales/tree/master/R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/scales/tree/master/R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378234809000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iKe9H6tbNLX_ZykYrgGr_\">https://github.com/hadley/scales/tree/master/R</a></div><div><br></div>for discrete color scales, ie a discrete variable actually inside the aesthetic: <div>\n\n<br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/scales/raw/master/R/pal-hue.r\" style=\"color:rgb(17,65,112)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/scales/raw/master/R/pal-hue.r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378234809000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2FmL4ZGiG9cv1_1pN5G8JU\">https://github.com/hadley/scales/raw/master/R/pal-hue.r</a></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## source the above function, though R seems unable to source an https</div>\n\n<div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## so cut and paste will probably have to work</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\n\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## you get the colors which can then be used in ggplots scale_manual() via:</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\n\nhue_pal()(5) </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\n\n## easy way to look at the colors</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## install.packages(&quot;gridExtra&quot;)</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\n\nlibrary(gridExtra) </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><div><div><div>grid.colorstrip(hue_pal()(5)) </div></div></div></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\n\ngrid.colorstrip(hue_pal()(5)[c(1, 3, 5)]) </div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
